WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
We would love to do a rapid fire,

2
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:05.490
get into many of our favorite movies that you were in,

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.190
and if you could share any fun facts about them,

4
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.767
we would be so delighted in something we call

5
00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.496
"Behind The Scenes".

6
00:00:12.496 --> 00:00:15.663
(audience applauding)

7
00:00:16.994 --> 00:00:18.060
Okay, here's how it works,

8
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.110
we're going to show you a movie that you were in

9
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.390
and we would love for you to share a detail

10
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.060
and insider fly on the wall moment,

11
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.210
anything that comes to mind.

12
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.887
First up "St. Elmo's Fire".

13
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.900
Well, it was off set,

14
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.320
like what comes to me first is

15
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.652
I was renting a place out in Los Angeles

16
00:00:35.652 --> 00:00:40.423
and my next door neighbor was Betty Davis.

17
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:45.710 line:15%
And I never saw her until one night I had a few drinks

18
00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.820 line:15%
and I decided I'm going to go meet Betty Davis.

19
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.933 line:15%
And I went and I knocked on her door

20
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:54.310
and then I panicked and I just ran home.

21
00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.143
So I sort of,

22
00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:57.980
and that was it.

23
00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:58.933
I never met her.

24
00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:02.430
Okay "Mannequin"

25
00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.560
The first thing always jumps to my mind about "Mannequin"

26
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.258
is that I hated that motor,

27
00:01:07.258 --> 00:01:08.884
I had to ride a motorcycle in the movie

28
00:01:08.884 --> 00:01:09.717
and I couldn't ride it,

29
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:10.670 line:15%
I would just get so tense when I do it,

30
00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.391 line:15%
like my shoulders would tense up so much

31
00:01:12.391 --> 00:01:14.170 line:15%
that I crashed early on

32
00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.550 line:15%
and they realized that no, he's not joking,

33
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.840 line:15%
he can't ride the motorcycle

34
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.050 line:15%
and so they had to just hook it up with some rig

35
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.410
every time I rode it

36
00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.910
and so that I would be pulled along,

37
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.650
and have to like put a fan on me to blow my hair

38
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.770
and all this kind of stuff

39
00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.923
because I was so incapable of riding my motorcycle.

40
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.080
Okay "Less Than Zero".

41
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.220
I never read the book.

42
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.483
My big secret from "Less Than Zero" is I never read it,

43
00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.430 line:15%
which we would all sit around

44
00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:42.350 line:15%
and they would talk about the book and I would be like,

45
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.800 line:15%
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,

46
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.213 line:15%
and I'm like, I have no idea what they're talking about.

47
00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.610 line:15%
But it was kind of good because the movie

48
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.770 line:15%
had nothing to do with the book.

49
00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.240
I don't think there was a single line

50
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.720
from the book in the movie,

51
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.030
but I did end up reading it decades later.

52
00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.350
But yeah, I wasn't much of a reader back then.

53
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.147
Okay, last one "Weekend at Bernie's".

54
00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.760
See the problem with telling stories

55
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.780
about Bernie is everything is on screen.

56
00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.430
Anything you could think of, it wasn't stupid enough.

57
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.480 line:15%
I remember it was like, let's staple,

58
00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.670 line:15%
let's say he has a toupee and staple his hair on him.

59
00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:18.170 line:15%
Like, okay, put a ball cap on him,

60
00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.380 line:15%
let's staple his head.

61
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.180 line:15%
You know, there's a scene when we were doing Monopoly,

62
00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.560 line:15%
playing Monopoly,

63
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.450 line:15%
I was playing Monopoly against dead Bernie

64
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.490
and it wasn't in the script I just had nothing to do

65
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.920
and I had been playing Monopoly at home the night before,

66
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.310
so I brought my Monopoly set to the work and I said,

67
00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:32.930
let me play Bernie in Monopoly,

68
00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.340
so we just had this Monopoly match,

69
00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.860
and it turned out to be great.

70
00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.440
You know, you can do anything to Bernie,

71
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.660
you could just drag him around,

72
00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.890
we realized the more you abuse his body,

73
00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:41.970
the funnier it's gonna be.

74
00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.850
There is a folklore if you will,

75
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.150
that my grandfather, John Barrymore,

76
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.620
they took his body out of the morgue, his friends,

77
00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.620
W.C Fields, Sadakichi Hartmann, John Decker, and Gene Fowler

78
00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.220
and they partied with him and it's this infamous story

79
00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.220
and they say, I have heard rumors

80
00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.480
that it was like a molecule of inspiration

81
00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.440
for "Weekend at Bernie's",

82
00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.130
did you ever hear that?

83
00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.690
That could well have been true,

84
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.190
but we did not have such a fine pedigree as that.

85
00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.133
We were just a couple of fools

86
00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:17.170
fooling around with this dead body, so no.

87
00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.170
As fabulous as they all were,

88
00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.760
they were total hedonists and party animals.

89
00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.780
And they were totally a bunch of hooligans.

90
00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.830
By the way, really quickly,

91
00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.460 line:15%
I didn't know this, is it true that you wore a wig

92
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.380 line:15%
at the very end of "Pretty in Pink"

93
00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.460 line:15%
because you had shaved you head

94
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.600 line:15%
for "Less Than Zero" already?

95
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.810
I was doing a play in New York and I shaved my head,

96
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.140
but I do have a wig on at the end of "Pretty in Pink",

97
00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.950
'cause we reshot the ending and so,

98
00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.480
when I go to Molly at the prom and tell her that I love her,

99
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.644
and I'm a terrible person and she's great,

100
00:03:45.644 --> 00:03:47.380
that was all a reshoot.

101
00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.790
They never die these movies

102
00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:53.237
And they can't, they're such a part of our history.

103
00:03:53.237 --> 00:03:56.220
(audience applauding)

104
00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.540
Andrew McCarthy "Brat, An 80's Story"

105
00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.610
is out now everywhere books are sold.

106
00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.121
Thank you, Andrew.

107
00:04:03.121 --> 00:04:05.788 line:15%
(upbeat music)

